  "title": "Contents (Volume II, continued)",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "manual-582-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Contents · Volume II continued"
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This continuation page guides readers through the later Ahmad Shah, Adina Beg, Brar, Doaba, and Sirhind sequences across a long historical span."
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Bhai Taru Singh, Kaura Mal, Ahmad Shah, and Adina Beg"
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The page begins with Bhai Taru Singh, the slaughter of Jassu, the massacre at Parol and Kathua, two short continuation notices, the destined death of Lakhu and Shah Narat, Ram Rauni, the valour of Kaura Mal, Sri Amritsar, Ahmad Shah Abdali and Sukha Singh, Episode 123 continued, Adina Beg and Sodhi Vad Bhag Singh, the Marathas and the Khalsa Panth, Sadiq Beg's betrayal in friendship, and Gazdi the minister."
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Gilja Pathans, Mir Mannu, and the Brar sequence"
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A second cluster covers the whole of India and the Gilja Pathans, the maneuvers of Gilja Pathans and Singhs, Hathloo Singh Majhail, Bikaner, the Bangar region, Mit Singh the martyr, Mir Mannu, Mathura and Koel, the Ghallughara near Malerkotla, Kup, and nearby settlements, the rift between the Khalsa Panth and the Brars, another episode about the Brars, Kapoora Brar, the slaughter at Maida, and the robbing of Luxmi Narayan."
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Kasur, Dileramian, Doaba, Taruna Dal, and Sirhind"
    },
    {
      "id": "manual-582-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The closing section lists the first invasion on Kasur, Dileramian, Dileramian continued, the occupation of Doaba, a further occupation sequence, the Taruna Dal, both Budha Dal and Taruna Dal, the capture of Sir Buland Khan, the occupation of Sirhind and the slaughter of Ali Khan, another episode about Sirhind, the construction of a memorial at Sirhind, the occupation and handing over of Sirhind, the handing over of towns to the descendants of Bhai Bhagtu and Baba Phool, and the Khalsa Panth's occupation of both sides."
    }
  ],
